  <div class="section">
    <h2>Key Feature Importance Findings</h2>
    <p>Across all supervised learning methods, certain features consistently emerged as the strongest predictors of round outcomes:</p>
    
    <div class="features-grid">
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h4>🥇 Equipment Advantage</h4>
        <p>The difference in team equipment values was the #1 predictor across all boosting methods. Teams with superior weapon loadouts have significantly higher win probabilities.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h4>🥈 Player Count</h4>
        <p>Number of players alive on each team strongly predicts outcomes. Numerical superiority translates directly to higher win probability.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h4>🥉 Time Elapsed</h4>
        <p>Round phase matters significantly - early, mid, and late game dynamics affect team advantages and strategies differently.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h4>Health Metrics</h4>
        <p>Total and average HP per team provide additional predictive signal, indicating team condition and survivability.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h2>Unsupervised Learning Insights</h2>
    <div class="insights-container">
      <div class="insight-box">
        <h3>Clustering Results</h3>
        <p>K-Means and Hierarchical clustering identified <strong>two distinct player archetypes</strong> in professional CS2:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Entry Fraggers:</strong> High K/D ratios, elevated opening kill counts, aggressive engagement patterns</li>
          <li><strong>Support/Finishing Players:</strong> Higher survival rates, more kills after bomb planting, supportive positioning</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="insight-box">
        <h3>PCA Results</h3>
        <p>Principal Component Analysis reduced <strong>17 features to 2 components</strong> while retaining 70.3% of variance:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>PC1 (58.0%):</strong> Overall player activity and performance level</li>
          <li><strong>PC2 (12.3%):</strong> Aggressive vs supportive playstyle distinction</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h2>Dataset Comparison</h2>
    <table class="results-table">
